1
00:00:35,145 --> 00:00:36,305
[This drama is fictional
and bears no resemblance to reality]

2
00:00:36,305 --> 00:00:37,255
[Some scenes feature AI technology]

3
00:00:37,255 --> 00:00:38,545
[All child and animal scenes
followed strict safety guidelines]

4
00:00:42,001 --> 00:00:46,565
Everyone will be waiting for your cue.

5
00:00:50,617 --> 00:00:52,189
Go ahead.

6
00:01:02,565 --> 00:01:04,548
Ready...

7
00:01:07,752 --> 00:01:09,596
Action!

8
00:01:11,716 --> 00:01:13,514
[Episode 8]
Buy a paper!

9
00:01:13,514 --> 00:01:15,207
Take one!

10
00:01:15,207 --> 00:01:17,318
Hello.

11
00:01:17,318 --> 00:01:19,209
What do you think?

12
00:01:19,209 --> 00:01:23,472
Not under Wolhajeong's lights,
but here under the moonlight.

13
00:01:23,472 --> 00:01:24,776
I'm not sure.

14
00:01:24,776 --> 00:01:28,946
From every angle, you seem free of all worries.

15
00:01:30,591 --> 00:01:32,780
Let me see.

16
00:01:34,379 --> 00:01:37,575
From every angle...

17
00:01:37,575 --> 00:01:39,672
Truly beautiful.

18
00:01:41,936 --> 00:01:45,820
I mean myself, reflected in your eyes.

19
00:01:48,269 --> 00:01:51,695
How are you always joking?

20
00:01:59,573 --> 00:02:01,321
<i>It suits you well.</i>

21
00:02:14,352 --> 00:02:16,395
Oh Ha Na!

22
00:02:18,674 --> 00:02:21,020
Everyone, stop filming!

23
00:02:23,235 --> 00:02:24,791
What's with her?

24
00:02:25,418 --> 00:02:28,761
- Come with me.
- Mom, stop! It hurts!

25
00:02:28,761 --> 00:02:30,153
Oh my!

26
00:02:30,839 --> 00:02:33,105
What do you think you're doing?

27
00:02:33,792 --> 00:02:34,382
Cut.

28
00:02:34,382 --> 00:02:38,482
You just stamped that contract. How dare you...

29
00:02:38,482 --> 00:02:41,326
Enough. People are watching.

30
00:02:41,966 --> 00:02:44,985
A scandal won't help you.

31
00:02:44,985 --> 00:02:50,085
As a mom shutting down a shoot,
or a CEO who lost her renewal.

32
00:03:04,295 --> 00:03:06,774
Surprise!

33
00:03:07,542 --> 00:03:09,822
Pretty good acting, right?

34
00:03:12,868 --> 00:03:16,485
I didn't expect Yu Geon
and the director to step in.

35
00:03:17,159 --> 00:03:18,686
Right, Ha Na?

36
00:03:18,686 --> 00:03:20,520
Hey, smile.

37
00:03:21,408 --> 00:03:22,825
Everyone!

38
00:03:22,825 --> 00:03:26,746
This was a surprise event Ha Na and I prepared.

39
00:03:26,746 --> 00:03:30,699
This is Ha Na's first starring film.

40
00:03:30,699 --> 00:03:32,799
We couldn't just let it pass.

41
00:03:32,799 --> 00:03:34,778
Sorry if we scared you.

42
00:03:34,778 --> 00:03:36,460
Sorry!

43
00:03:37,885 --> 00:03:43,029
It was all an act to give you padded jackets.

44
00:03:43,029 --> 00:03:47,893
It'll get cold soon, so stay warm on set.

45
00:03:47,893 --> 00:03:50,611
Director Kang will hand them out.

46
00:03:50,611 --> 00:03:53,380
Please take good care of Ha Na.

47
00:03:53,380 --> 00:03:55,340
There he comes.

48
00:03:56,856 --> 00:03:58,787
Let's take a short break.

49
00:03:58,787 --> 00:04:00,762
Hello. The jackets are here!

50
00:04:00,762 --> 00:04:02,389
They're free!

51
00:04:02,389 --> 00:04:04,216
An Su Hui!

52
00:04:04,216 --> 00:04:05,843
- Oh Ha Na!
- Oh Ha Na!

53
00:04:05,843 --> 00:04:07,247
- An Su Hui!
- An Su Hui!

54
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:08,933
- Oh Ha Na!
- Oh Ha Na!

55
00:04:08,933 --> 00:04:11,010
- Stay warm.
- An Su Hui!

56
00:04:11,010 --> 00:04:12,649
- Oh Ha Na!
- Oh Ha Na!

57
00:04:12,649 --> 00:04:14,663
- An Su Hui!
- An Su Hui!

58
00:04:15,410 --> 00:04:17,487
Here you go!

59
00:04:17,487 --> 00:04:19,484
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

60
00:04:19,484 --> 00:04:21,184
My pleasure.

61
00:04:22,661 --> 00:04:25,736
- We need to talk.
- That's what I wanted.

62
00:04:26,775 --> 00:04:27,993
Yeah.

63
00:04:27,993 --> 00:04:29,887
Stay warm.

64
00:04:29,887 --> 00:04:31,706
Stay warm!

65
00:04:36,374 --> 00:04:39,259
I'm warm-toned. Black isn't my color.

66
00:04:39,259 --> 00:04:42,297
"Warm-toned?" More like one-tenth-ton.

67
00:04:43,641 --> 00:04:46,838
I really thought we were shutting down.

68
00:04:46,838 --> 00:04:49,802
What kind of surprise is that terrifying?

69
00:04:49,802 --> 00:04:51,934
Maybe we really will shut down.

70
00:04:51,934 --> 00:04:53,170
What?

71
00:04:53,830 --> 00:04:57,726
The real act was pretending it was an act.

72
00:04:58,486 --> 00:05:01,697
Seok Gi heard everything.

73
00:05:01,697 --> 00:05:04,284
<i>Enough. People are watching.</i>

74
00:05:04,284 --> 00:05:06,332
<i>A scandal won't help you.</i>

75
00:05:06,332 --> 00:05:10,496
<i>As a mom shutting down a shoot,
or a CEO who lost her renewal.</i>

76
00:05:10,496 --> 00:05:12,426
<i>Surprise!</i>

77
00:05:12,426 --> 00:05:14,126
<i>Pretty good acting, right?</i>

78
00:05:14,126 --> 00:05:15,337
No way.

79
00:05:15,337 --> 00:05:17,163
I knew something was off.

80
00:05:17,163 --> 00:05:21,163
A star like Oh Ha Na joins,
and not one article?

81
00:05:21,163 --> 00:05:23,227
She just went on hiatus.

82
00:05:23,227 --> 00:05:26,514
Burnout? Please.

83
00:05:26,514 --> 00:05:32,496
So the whole "surprise event" thing was a lie?

84
00:05:32,496 --> 00:05:36,120
And I was worshipping them like an idiot.

85
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:39,599
What if their fight blows up on all of us?

86
00:05:39,599 --> 00:05:42,129
What if the whole project falls apart...

87
00:05:42,129 --> 00:05:44,074
Enough with the nonsense.

88
00:05:44,074 --> 00:05:46,727
Stop stirring things up.

89
00:05:46,727 --> 00:05:49,880
It hasn't even happened. Cut it out.

90
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:51,944
Just keep the crew quiet.

91
00:05:51,944 --> 00:05:53,513
Got it.

92
00:05:54,367 --> 00:05:57,838
Badmouthing the set outside
only makes us look bad.

93
00:05:57,838 --> 00:06:00,699
- Yeah.
- Let's just do our jobs. Come on.

94
00:06:00,699 --> 00:06:01,883
- Yes.
- Let's go.

95
00:06:01,883 --> 00:06:03,596
Wait.

96
00:06:04,798 --> 00:06:07,902
Cute little stunt you're pulling here.

97
00:06:07,902 --> 00:06:12,282
You thought once filming started, I'd be stuck?

98
00:06:12,282 --> 00:06:14,229
Do you know who I am?

99
00:06:14,229 --> 00:06:15,731
Shut this shoot down now!

100
00:06:15,731 --> 00:06:17,916
Everything stops until I say so.

101
00:06:17,916 --> 00:06:19,213
Mom.

102
00:06:19,213 --> 00:06:23,796
CEO An, you don't have that authority.

103
00:06:23,796 --> 00:06:25,967
No, I don't.

104
00:06:25,967 --> 00:06:29,283
But I do have power.

105
00:06:30,183 --> 00:06:32,720
I won't accept Oh Ha Na.

106
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:34,987
Until she's out, I'm boycotting this.

107
00:06:34,987 --> 00:06:36,780
Get in, Yu Geon.

108
00:06:38,618 --> 00:06:40,248
Get in!

109
00:06:40,248 --> 00:06:42,574
You're not filming this.

110
00:06:42,574 --> 00:06:44,498
Fine.

111
00:06:44,498 --> 00:06:46,364
Then I'll...

112
00:06:47,041 --> 00:06:49,894
I'll withdraw from the project, CEO An.

113
00:06:49,894 --> 00:06:51,317
- Sim Yu Geon.
- Yu Geon.

114
00:06:51,317 --> 00:06:52,384
What?

115
00:06:52,384 --> 00:06:53,934
You know what that means?

116
00:06:53,934 --> 00:06:58,331
You'll never set foot in this industry again.

117
00:06:58,331 --> 00:07:00,189
I don't care.

118
00:07:00,189 --> 00:07:04,644
It was never my place anyway.

119
00:07:08,638 --> 00:07:10,407
Sorry, Yi Jae.

120
00:07:11,172 --> 00:07:13,170
I'm sorry, Soo Bin.

121
00:07:21,555 --> 00:07:23,452
Let's do that, then.

122
00:07:23,452 --> 00:07:26,489
Directors, find another male lead.

123
00:07:26,489 --> 00:07:30,136
With Ha Na's rumors, that won't be easy.

124
00:07:30,136 --> 00:07:31,842
Ma'am!

125
00:07:33,603 --> 00:07:36,306
The jackets are all handed out.

126
00:07:36,306 --> 00:07:39,025
I also left the directors' jackets...

127
00:07:40,272 --> 00:07:42,376
- Let's go.
- Yes, ma'am.

128
00:07:42,376 --> 00:07:44,076
Hurry.

129
00:07:44,744 --> 00:07:46,548
Yu Geon.

130
00:08:00,742 --> 00:08:02,779
Ha Na.

131
00:08:02,779 --> 00:08:07,399
I told you I think ahead,
even about what I can do next.

132
00:08:07,399 --> 00:08:09,423
Watch and learn.

133
00:08:09,423 --> 00:08:14,288
It all happened because of
that stupid rebellious attitude of yours.

134
00:08:29,588 --> 00:08:32,835
Let's call off today's shoot.

135
00:08:40,430 --> 00:08:41,437
Sorry.

136
00:08:41,437 --> 00:08:43,321
This is all because of me...

137
00:08:46,354 --> 00:08:48,778
It's not your fault.

138
00:08:48,778 --> 00:08:50,630
It's okay.

139
00:09:07,065 --> 00:09:08,455
Hello.

140
00:09:08,455 --> 00:09:12,737
I'm Nam Ye Seo,
your new producer starting today.

141
00:09:12,737 --> 00:09:15,745
Hello, I'm Seo In Uk.

142
00:09:17,818 --> 00:09:21,384
These are the final three for Moo Gyeom.

143
00:09:22,145 --> 00:09:24,200
Let's pick one.

144
00:09:26,003 --> 00:09:28,286
You came ready like you were waiting for this.

145
00:09:28,286 --> 00:09:30,243
I didn't find them.

146
00:09:30,243 --> 00:09:33,454
They wanted in before Sim Yu Geon.

147
00:09:33,454 --> 00:09:36,099
Is recasting really our best option?

148
00:09:36,099 --> 00:09:37,391
More than best.

149
00:09:37,391 --> 00:09:40,034
It may be for the better.

150
00:09:40,034 --> 00:09:41,078
Exactly.

151
00:09:41,078 --> 00:09:44,651
And he's the hottest actor in Korea right now.

152
00:09:44,651 --> 00:09:46,067
Geum Seong Moo.

153
00:09:46,067 --> 00:09:47,917
Geum Seong Moo?

154
00:09:48,595 --> 00:09:50,805
- Why?
- I mean...

155
00:09:50,805 --> 00:09:53,282
If he's that hot, isn't he busy?

156
00:09:53,282 --> 00:09:55,319
He must have projects lined up.

157
00:09:55,319 --> 00:09:59,538
If the script is good, actors line up for it.

158
00:09:59,538 --> 00:10:01,383
You're too kind.

159
00:10:01,383 --> 00:10:02,823
So...

160
00:10:02,823 --> 00:10:03,886
Let's wrap this up.

161
00:10:03,886 --> 00:10:08,755
We're burning money as we speak.

162
00:10:08,755 --> 00:10:13,120
CEO An secured more funding in LA

163
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:15,908
and even closed pre-sales.

164
00:10:15,908 --> 00:10:19,198
Doesn't that mean
this project means more to her now?

165
00:10:19,198 --> 00:10:20,342
Yeah.

166
00:10:20,342 --> 00:10:21,351
So?

167
00:10:21,351 --> 00:10:24,384
CEO An has no plans to drop Yu Geon.

168
00:10:25,257 --> 00:10:27,661
She used him as a bluff.

169
00:10:27,661 --> 00:10:30,517
For what?

170
00:10:43,736 --> 00:10:46,394
[Contract for Pop Culture Artists]

171
00:10:51,387 --> 00:10:54,244
You didn't call me here to end my contract?

172
00:10:54,244 --> 00:10:58,362
You really underestimated me.

173
00:10:58,362 --> 00:11:01,928
Did you think you could break this contract?

174
00:11:01,928 --> 00:11:03,952
Did you forget what I told you?

175
00:11:03,952 --> 00:11:08,026
That scrap of paper owns you, body and soul.

176
00:11:26,366 --> 00:11:28,564
I'll renew my contract.

177
00:11:28,564 --> 00:11:30,062
Leave Yu Geon alone.

178
00:11:30,062 --> 00:11:31,529
Good.

179
00:11:32,135 --> 00:11:35,109
Your contract is in his hand.

180
00:11:35,109 --> 00:11:37,712
- Stamp it.
- You don't have to do this.

181
00:11:37,712 --> 00:11:40,712
I'll put everything back the way it was.

182
00:11:42,446 --> 00:11:44,030
How?

183
00:11:44,030 --> 00:11:46,691
Are you naive, or just clueless?

184
00:11:46,691 --> 00:11:49,910
Mom wanted me from the start.

185
00:11:51,137 --> 00:11:52,561
And Mom,

186
00:11:52,561 --> 00:11:54,948
I wasn't doing this film because of him.

187
00:11:54,948 --> 00:11:57,990
I found the script myself.
I even auditioned for it.

188
00:11:57,990 --> 00:12:00,747
He just happened to be there after I joined.

189
00:12:00,747 --> 00:12:02,100
Annoyingly enough.

190
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:04,614
Then I had good instincts.

191
00:12:04,614 --> 00:12:08,464
I picked the right hostage
and brought you back.

192
00:12:08,464 --> 00:12:10,588
Give her the contract.

193
00:12:10,588 --> 00:12:12,283
Give it to me.

194
00:12:26,934 --> 00:12:31,951
I trust this paper more than your feelings.

195
00:12:32,558 --> 00:12:34,880
You're still in my palm.

196
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:37,495
What can you possibly do?

197
00:12:44,592 --> 00:12:46,913
[Gyeongseong Love Song]

198
00:12:46,913 --> 00:12:52,056
Why did Nan Young risk her life
to save Moo Gyeom?

199
00:12:52,694 --> 00:12:54,644
She ran off to live as herself.

200
00:12:54,644 --> 00:12:56,464
What an idiot.

201
00:12:57,414 --> 00:13:00,720
Maybe that was how she saved herself.

202
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:02,284
Ha Na.

203
00:13:02,284 --> 00:13:03,680
They say when you're in love,

204
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:07,528
your eyes, nose, and lips
all turn toward that person.

205
00:13:07,528 --> 00:13:09,447
You know what that means?

206
00:13:09,447 --> 00:13:13,226
You look at their face more than your own.

207
00:13:13,226 --> 00:13:17,902
So when they smile, you smile too.

208
00:13:17,902 --> 00:13:22,735
And when they cry, you realize you cry too.

209
00:13:24,912 --> 00:13:27,646
Is that why it hurts this much?

210
00:13:28,379 --> 00:13:30,116
Ha Na.

211
00:13:30,116 --> 00:13:32,873
I'm sorry, but please stop talking.

212
00:13:32,873 --> 00:13:36,780
We've gotten on Olympic Expressway
three times now.

213
00:13:37,834 --> 00:13:39,250
Gosh...

214
00:13:39,250 --> 00:13:41,744
Sorry. Can you pull over somewhere?

215
00:13:41,744 --> 00:13:42,948
I can't pull over.

216
00:13:42,948 --> 00:13:44,934
There are too many cars.

217
00:13:44,934 --> 00:13:48,157
I'm actually scared of driving.

218
00:13:49,115 --> 00:13:51,026
How much farther?

219
00:13:51,026 --> 00:13:53,666
Check the GPS, please.

220
00:13:55,246 --> 00:13:59,350
I think Crow should be played
by someone everyone knows.

221
00:13:59,350 --> 00:14:02,004
- Yeah.
- He's the independence army leader.

222
00:14:02,004 --> 00:14:04,034
His entrance needs impact.

223
00:14:04,034 --> 00:14:07,891
Someone who makes the audience gasp
the second they see him.

224
00:14:07,891 --> 00:14:10,216
But it's a small role, so it might be tough.

225
00:14:10,216 --> 00:14:13,756
Then why not offer it as a cameo?

226
00:14:13,756 --> 00:14:16,664
Is now really the time to discuss a cameo?

227
00:14:16,664 --> 00:14:18,151
We don't even have a lead.

228
00:14:18,151 --> 00:14:19,840
We should do what we can.

229
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:21,429
You said we're burning money.

230
00:14:21,429 --> 00:14:23,982
The articles are out!

231
00:14:30,085 --> 00:14:32,016
[Who Is Sim Yu Geon, Oh Ha Na's Leading Man?]

232
00:14:32,016 --> 00:14:34,305
Topline released these.

233
00:14:34,305 --> 00:14:36,420
Yu Geon got an article...

234
00:14:36,420 --> 00:14:38,525
We need an official release too.

235
00:14:38,525 --> 00:14:40,588
- Get on it.
- Yes, sir.

236
00:14:43,631 --> 00:14:45,240
<i>Please help me.</i>

237
00:14:45,240 --> 00:14:48,096
<i>So I can live as Oh Ha Na, not her daughter.</i>

238
00:14:48,096 --> 00:14:51,514
<i>If Nan Young can be
my first step toward independence,</i>

239
00:14:51,514 --> 00:14:54,216
<i>it'll mean everything to me.</i>

240
00:14:55,602 --> 00:14:58,335
So her first step toward independence is gone.

241
00:14:58,335 --> 00:15:00,996
Will she be okay?

242
00:15:00,996 --> 00:15:03,003
She will be.

243
00:15:03,003 --> 00:15:05,686
Either way, she chose this herself.

244
00:15:05,686 --> 00:15:08,150
To protect what matters to her.

245
00:15:12,808 --> 00:15:14,561
[Who Is Sim Yu Geon, Oh Ha Na's Leading Man?]

246
00:15:14,561 --> 00:15:16,634
[Oh Ha Na Makes Her Film Debut
in Ian Woo's Next Project]

247
00:15:24,488 --> 00:15:26,795
[Expiration date: Ten thousand years]

248
00:15:32,807 --> 00:15:35,540
<i>You were desperate enough
to sign that insane contract.</i>

249
00:15:35,540 --> 00:15:38,557
<i>Why quit now?</i>

250
00:15:41,295 --> 00:15:45,676
<i>You should've stayed right by my side
and shown my mom properly.</i>

251
00:15:46,301 --> 00:15:48,841
<i>That there's absolutely no such thing as love.</i>

252
00:16:58,736 --> 00:17:01,422
Hwa Yeon!

253
00:17:07,696 --> 00:17:10,208
Hwa Yeon!

254
00:17:11,782 --> 00:17:15,543
If she's not here, where the hell is she?

255
00:17:20,597 --> 00:17:24,519
When I find you, you're dead!

256
00:17:28,251 --> 00:17:30,202
Woo Soo Bin!

257
00:17:30,202 --> 00:17:32,375
Woo Soo Bin!

258
00:17:34,447 --> 00:17:36,393
Woo Soo Bin!

259
00:17:53,490 --> 00:17:55,218
Evidence video.

260
00:17:55,218 --> 00:17:57,770
So no one thinks I did this.

261
00:18:01,895 --> 00:18:03,203
Long time no see.

262
00:18:03,203 --> 00:18:05,463
Yeah. 20 years.

263
00:18:05,463 --> 00:18:08,698
Get out in 20 seconds before I call the cops.

264
00:18:08,698 --> 00:18:13,468
An invited guest doesn't break down the door.

265
00:18:16,342 --> 00:18:18,885
Looks like the same goes for you.

266
00:18:20,574 --> 00:18:23,378
Coming to a house when no one's home.

267
00:18:23,378 --> 00:18:27,002
Why are you here anyway?

268
00:18:27,002 --> 00:18:31,236
I'm funding Soo Bin's movie.

269
00:18:31,236 --> 00:18:34,202
I had something urgent to discuss.

270
00:18:34,202 --> 00:18:36,078
What?

271
00:18:36,078 --> 00:18:37,180
Hey.

272
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:40,058
You really are crazy.

273
00:18:40,058 --> 00:18:42,519
That's why I dated a bastard like you.

274
00:18:42,519 --> 00:18:44,062
I didn't even know you were married.

275
00:18:44,062 --> 00:18:45,673
Still bitter about that?

276
00:18:45,673 --> 00:18:48,191
You got pregnant
and told me to divorce my wife.

277
00:18:48,191 --> 00:18:50,611
You locked me in a clinic so I couldn't end it.

278
00:18:50,611 --> 00:18:53,008
Fine, fine.

279
00:18:53,008 --> 00:18:56,781
I made a huge mistake back then.

280
00:18:57,398 --> 00:19:02,234
You could've had the baby in secret...

281
00:19:02,234 --> 00:19:04,625
and disappeared.

282
00:19:04,625 --> 00:19:07,003
No one would've cared.

283
00:19:07,681 --> 00:19:11,314
But I showed you useless mercy.

284
00:19:16,261 --> 00:19:20,061
That's how much I liked you.

285
00:19:21,445 --> 00:19:23,528
Su Hui.

286
00:19:23,528 --> 00:19:26,253
I'll repay that kindness!

287
00:19:39,736 --> 00:19:41,433
Nice.

288
00:19:41,433 --> 00:19:43,815
Brings back memories.

289
00:19:58,042 --> 00:20:00,472
- I can't wait to get back on set.
- You like it that much?

290
00:20:00,472 --> 00:20:03,770
Of course. It's so much fun.

291
00:20:03,770 --> 00:20:05,118
Yeah?

292
00:20:08,250 --> 00:20:10,130
What is this?

293
00:20:11,684 --> 00:20:13,602
Wait here.

294
00:20:17,705 --> 00:20:21,118
I should've had you thrown in jail back then!

295
00:20:22,497 --> 00:20:25,349
What are you two doing here?

296
00:20:27,004 --> 00:20:28,663
Yi Jae. Go home.

297
00:20:28,663 --> 00:20:30,236
Okay.

298
00:20:31,703 --> 00:20:33,644
Oh my...

299
00:20:36,254 --> 00:20:38,444
Where's your mom?

300
00:20:38,444 --> 00:20:41,197
I told you clearly.

301
00:20:41,197 --> 00:20:42,941
Don't look for her again.

302
00:20:42,941 --> 00:20:45,820
This time, you'll answer.

303
00:20:45,820 --> 00:20:48,406
Where's your mom?

304
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:52,750
Hey.

305
00:20:58,328 --> 00:20:59,363
Are you insane?

306
00:20:59,363 --> 00:21:02,326
It's attempted murder!

307
00:21:04,075 --> 00:21:06,591
Get out. Both of you.

308
00:21:08,186 --> 00:21:10,756
You said you'd be a stain on my life forever.

309
00:21:10,756 --> 00:21:12,386
And this is your plan?

310
00:21:12,386 --> 00:21:15,229
Siding with the mom who abandoned you?

311
00:21:15,229 --> 00:21:17,853
Have you no shame?

312
00:21:18,536 --> 00:21:22,099
What the hell is this scumbag saying?

313
00:21:22,099 --> 00:21:24,556
I never spent a day as his mom.

314
00:21:24,556 --> 00:21:27,016
So don't call me that.

315
00:21:27,016 --> 00:21:29,300
I came here as Ha Na's mom.

316
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:31,480
Exactly.

317
00:21:31,480 --> 00:21:33,914
So get out.

318
00:21:33,914 --> 00:21:36,869
Neither of you is anything to me.

319
00:21:37,801 --> 00:21:39,568
Then...

320
00:21:40,481 --> 00:21:44,242
You'll make Hwa Yeon
live on the run forever too?

321
00:21:44,242 --> 00:21:46,888
Just like you?

322
00:21:46,888 --> 00:21:50,905
She's not running.
I'm keeping her safe from you.

323
00:22:07,683 --> 00:22:12,528
If you don't want her hurt,
send her back to me.

324
00:22:20,818 --> 00:22:23,891
I shouldn't have fixed you.

325
00:22:24,652 --> 00:22:28,282
Things that are broken once

326
00:22:28,282 --> 00:22:32,242
- are hard to fix completely...
- Father!

327
00:22:33,524 --> 00:22:34,668
You're right.

328
00:22:34,668 --> 00:22:39,911
Just because you fixed my leg
doesn't mean you fixed my life.

329
00:22:39,911 --> 00:22:45,117
Soo Bin is the one
who put my life back together.

330
00:23:02,376 --> 00:23:04,998
That bastard still lives like that?

331
00:23:04,998 --> 00:23:08,742
And you still live like this?

332
00:23:08,742 --> 00:23:11,789
I didn't come here to watch this mess.

333
00:23:11,789 --> 00:23:13,915
Hey.

334
00:23:13,915 --> 00:23:16,986
Why did you cast Ha Na?

335
00:23:16,986 --> 00:23:20,359
You came all this way to ask me that?

336
00:23:20,359 --> 00:23:23,693
What did you think I was after?

337
00:23:23,693 --> 00:23:27,083
You wouldn't take her when I offered.

338
00:23:27,083 --> 00:23:31,156
So why cast her the moment she left me?

339
00:23:32,319 --> 00:23:36,895
You and my father really are alike.

340
00:23:36,895 --> 00:23:39,293
- What?
- Maybe that's why

341
00:23:39,293 --> 00:23:41,506
Ha Na and I are alike.

342
00:23:41,506 --> 00:23:43,193
Though we weren't raised together.

343
00:23:43,193 --> 00:23:44,230
Hey!

344
00:23:44,230 --> 00:23:46,787
That's exactly why I came here.

345
00:23:46,787 --> 00:23:52,559
Don't you dare tell Ha Na
you're siblings or family.

346
00:23:52,559 --> 00:23:54,584
Or I don't know what I'll do.

347
00:23:54,584 --> 00:23:58,712
A director cast an actress in a movie.

348
00:23:59,307 --> 00:24:01,779
You're reading a lot into it.

349
00:24:02,513 --> 00:24:05,549
This is an important time for her.

350
00:24:05,549 --> 00:24:08,583
So don't get swept up in pointless emotions.

351
00:24:08,583 --> 00:24:12,399
Just finish the movie.

352
00:24:34,436 --> 00:24:35,900
Soo Bin.

353
00:24:35,900 --> 00:24:37,847
Are you okay?

354
00:24:39,241 --> 00:24:41,834
Yi Jae, I'm sorry.

355
00:24:42,907 --> 00:24:44,580
Give me a minute.

356
00:25:23,415 --> 00:25:25,158
Woo Soo Bin.

357
00:25:56,410 --> 00:25:59,832
They say all happy families are alike,

358
00:25:59,832 --> 00:26:02,055
but every unhappy family

359
00:26:03,105 --> 00:26:05,228
has its own reason.

360
00:26:05,228 --> 00:26:06,559
<i>Hello.</i>

361
00:26:06,559 --> 00:26:08,340
<i>You must be Soo Bin.</i>

362
00:26:08,340 --> 00:26:09,803
<i>Say hello.</i>

363
00:26:09,803 --> 00:26:13,170
<i>This is your aunt and your uncle.</i>

364
00:26:13,170 --> 00:26:14,595
<i>Hello.</i>

365
00:26:14,595 --> 00:26:16,651
In our family,

366
00:26:16,651 --> 00:26:18,362
I was that reason.

367
00:26:26,021 --> 00:26:27,734
<i>It's An Su Hui.</i>

368
00:26:31,473 --> 00:26:33,280
<i>Look.</i>

369
00:26:33,280 --> 00:26:36,571
<i>He looks more like her every day.</i>

370
00:26:36,571 --> 00:26:39,369
<i>So she really is his mom?</i>

371
00:26:39,369 --> 00:26:42,694
<i>Her husband really is...</i>

372
00:26:43,314 --> 00:26:45,625
<i>Hwa Yeon is something else.</i>

373
00:26:45,625 --> 00:26:49,621
<i>Raising a child from his affair...</i>

374
00:26:49,621 --> 00:26:51,671
<i>So damn ignorant.</i>

375
00:26:51,671 --> 00:26:54,633
<i>Why would you say that crap to a kid?</i>

376
00:26:54,633 --> 00:26:57,091
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

377
00:26:57,091 --> 00:26:59,383
<i>I'm sorry...</i>

378
00:27:00,155 --> 00:27:04,460
<i>Soo Bin is my son.</i>

379
00:27:08,880 --> 00:27:12,923
<i>If you want your family that badly, go alone.</i>

380
00:27:12,923 --> 00:27:15,531
<i>And don't come back.</i>

381
00:27:16,144 --> 00:27:18,704
<i>No...</i>

382
00:27:19,464 --> 00:27:22,337
<i>I won't go again.</i>

383
00:27:22,950 --> 00:27:24,852
<i>I mean it.</i>

384
00:27:28,170 --> 00:27:29,982
That was when I realized.

385
00:27:32,253 --> 00:27:33,300
Some smiles...

386
00:27:33,300 --> 00:27:36,367
<i>Sweetie. You're awake?</i>

387
00:27:36,367 --> 00:27:38,567
look like crying.

388
00:27:40,057 --> 00:27:43,118
Every time Mom looked at me,

389
00:27:43,118 --> 00:27:45,082
she was crying.

390
00:28:04,972 --> 00:28:06,535
<i>Hey.</i>

391
00:28:12,369 --> 00:28:15,032
<i>Mom, who is he?</i>

392
00:28:17,592 --> 00:28:18,855
<i>Ha Na.</i>

393
00:28:18,855 --> 00:28:20,868
<i>Get inside!</i>

394
00:28:29,643 --> 00:28:31,376
<i>Who are you?</i>

395
00:28:32,204 --> 00:28:35,330
<i>Hello. I'm Woo Soo Bin.</i>

396
00:28:41,673 --> 00:28:43,403
<i>What are you doing here?</i>

397
00:28:43,403 --> 00:28:45,241
<i>Who sent you?</i>

398
00:28:45,241 --> 00:28:47,980
<i>Woo Cheol Gyu? Or that woman?</i>

399
00:28:47,980 --> 00:28:48,999
<i>What?</i>

400
00:28:48,999 --> 00:28:50,520
<i>They don't want you anymore?</i>

401
00:28:50,520 --> 00:28:51,875
<i>I came alone.</i>

402
00:28:51,875 --> 00:28:54,682
<i>My mom cries every day because of me.</i>

403
00:28:54,682 --> 00:28:58,969
<i>If I'm gone, Dad won't get mad,
and Mom won't cry.</i>

404
00:28:58,969 --> 00:29:00,286
<i>So what?</i>

405
00:29:00,286 --> 00:29:02,432
<i>Please raise me.</i>

406
00:29:02,432 --> 00:29:04,957
<i>I'm good at school. I listen well.</i>

407
00:29:04,957 --> 00:29:09,445
<i>If you just raise me, I'll grow up well.</i>

408
00:29:09,445 --> 00:29:12,278
<i>- Where's your house? Lead the way.
- No!</i>

409
00:29:12,278 --> 00:29:14,776
<i>Please take me in!</i>

410
00:29:14,776 --> 00:29:16,858
<i>- Keep it down!
- Please!</i>

411
00:29:16,858 --> 00:29:18,616
<i>Please.</i>

412
00:29:18,616 --> 00:29:21,100
<i>- Quiet!
- Please take me in...</i>

413
00:29:21,100 --> 00:29:23,531
<i>Please.</i>

414
00:29:23,531 --> 00:29:25,856
<i>Please take me in...</i>

415
00:29:27,017 --> 00:29:28,840
<i>Oh my...</i>

416
00:29:28,840 --> 00:29:31,097
<i>Please take me in...</i>

417
00:29:31,097 --> 00:29:33,286
<i>- Stop it.
- Please.</i>

418
00:29:45,580 --> 00:29:47,007
<i>Get out.</i>

419
00:29:52,369 --> 00:29:55,186
<i>This is why he came to me!</i>

420
00:29:55,186 --> 00:29:56,623
<i>He begged me to take him in.</i>

421
00:29:56,623 --> 00:29:57,929
<i>Can you believe it?</i>

422
00:29:57,929 --> 00:29:59,256
<i>Great.</i>

423
00:29:59,256 --> 00:30:00,906
<i>Then you raise him.</i>

424
00:30:00,906 --> 00:30:04,046
<i>I don't need this rotten kid either.</i>

425
00:30:04,046 --> 00:30:06,761
<i>Cheol Gyu! I have my own family now.</i>

426
00:30:06,761 --> 00:30:09,556
<i>How am I supposed to raise him?</i>

427
00:30:09,556 --> 00:30:12,865
<i>- Mom...
- I'm not your mom!</i>

428
00:30:12,865 --> 00:30:15,188
<i>Come here, Soo Bin.</i>

429
00:30:20,138 --> 00:30:23,368
<i>Where did you go?</i>

430
00:30:23,368 --> 00:30:27,061
<i>Do you know how worried I was?</i>

431
00:30:27,061 --> 00:30:28,848
<i>I just...</i>

432
00:30:28,848 --> 00:30:32,554
<i>I thought I was the reason you cried.</i>

433
00:30:33,952 --> 00:30:35,939
<i>Soo Bin...</i>

434
00:30:35,939 --> 00:30:38,274
<i>You make me cry,</i>

435
00:30:38,274 --> 00:30:42,042
<i>and you make me smile like this too.</i>

436
00:30:42,042 --> 00:30:44,325
<i>Because you're my son.</i>

437
00:30:48,135 --> 00:30:49,866
<i>Mom...</i>

438
00:30:49,866 --> 00:30:52,575
<i>Don't cry, my son.</i>

439
00:31:10,491 --> 00:31:12,937
After that day...

440
00:31:12,937 --> 00:31:16,208
my whole world was just pitch-black darkness.

441
00:31:22,861 --> 00:31:26,145
When I thought I was better off in the dark...

442
00:31:29,321 --> 00:31:31,364
That's when I met you.

443
00:31:34,611 --> 00:31:37,597
Why does this story end with you?

444
00:31:38,431 --> 00:31:40,125
Maybe...

445
00:31:40,944 --> 00:31:43,707
Because you were the first person

446
00:31:44,300 --> 00:31:46,347
who lit up my world.

447
00:31:48,764 --> 00:31:50,397
Woo Soo Bin.

448
00:31:52,088 --> 00:31:54,708
Because of you...

449
00:31:54,708 --> 00:31:59,438
all my bad memories turned into love.

450
00:32:00,688 --> 00:32:06,174
This scar now means I loved you that much.

451
00:32:06,174 --> 00:32:11,034
And movies aren't some dream
I never got to have.

452
00:32:11,034 --> 00:32:13,879
They're a dream I share with you.

453
00:32:15,722 --> 00:32:17,922
When it rains...

454
00:32:19,836 --> 00:32:22,792
I don't think of our breakup anymore.

455
00:32:22,792 --> 00:32:25,545
I think of our kiss.

456
00:32:28,425 --> 00:32:33,034
How could this not be love?

457
00:32:38,605 --> 00:32:43,083
That's the greatest comfort I've ever had.

458
00:32:43,083 --> 00:32:44,775
Really?

459
00:33:49,283 --> 00:33:51,186
Sorry.

460
00:33:51,186 --> 00:33:54,335
It's been so long since someone was next to me.

461
00:33:57,335 --> 00:33:58,985
What?

462
00:33:58,985 --> 00:34:00,355
What time is it?

463
00:34:00,355 --> 00:34:02,359
Can I sleep a little longer?

464
00:34:03,642 --> 00:34:05,331
"So long?"

465
00:34:08,087 --> 00:34:10,487
Wake me up later.

466
00:34:12,809 --> 00:34:15,160
"So long?"

467
00:34:15,160 --> 00:34:17,167
I don't know.

468
00:34:20,451 --> 00:34:21,536
How long has it been?

469
00:34:21,536 --> 00:34:25,056
Why are you doing this so early?

470
00:34:25,056 --> 00:34:28,609
I said, how long has it been?

471
00:34:28,609 --> 00:34:30,036
- I don't know.
- Hey.

472
00:34:30,036 --> 00:34:31,726
- Ju Yi Jae!
- Yeah?

473
00:34:31,726 --> 00:34:33,596
- Was it him?
- Huh?

474
00:34:33,596 --> 00:34:36,592
- I'm asking you.
- That tickles.

475
00:34:36,592 --> 00:34:38,759
- Answer me.
- It tickles!

476
00:34:43,230 --> 00:34:46,254
That war-zone love guy?

477
00:34:46,977 --> 00:34:48,525
Right?

478
00:34:50,703 --> 00:34:53,620
He was good at cutting apples too.

479
00:34:53,620 --> 00:34:55,000
What?

480
00:34:58,207 --> 00:35:00,137
How good?

481
00:35:00,137 --> 00:35:02,455
Could he make apple bunnies too?

482
00:35:03,810 --> 00:35:05,281
Today's finally the scene.

483
00:35:05,281 --> 00:35:07,546
Nan Young falls for Moo Gyeom at first sight.

484
00:35:07,546 --> 00:35:09,232
I can't wait.

485
00:35:09,232 --> 00:35:12,301
Why? Did you fall for him at first sight too?

486
00:35:12,301 --> 00:35:14,678
How long are you keeping this up?

487
00:35:14,678 --> 00:35:16,090
When are you going to tell me?

488
00:35:16,090 --> 00:35:19,363
I told you, we only dated for a bit.

489
00:35:19,363 --> 00:35:21,953
He was an acting major...

490
00:35:21,953 --> 00:35:24,216
So he was hot.

491
00:35:24,216 --> 00:35:25,987
Of course.

492
00:35:26,857 --> 00:35:29,481
He was cute back then. Not now.

493
00:35:29,481 --> 00:35:32,590
You still keep in touch?

494
00:35:32,590 --> 00:35:34,573
No, no!

495
00:35:34,573 --> 00:35:40,391
We just dated in college,
so we had mutual friends.

496
00:35:40,391 --> 00:35:43,661
Anyway, he kept helping me on my student films.

497
00:35:43,661 --> 00:35:45,781
It just happened. That's all.

498
00:35:45,781 --> 00:35:48,545
"It just happened?" That's the dangerous part.

499
00:35:48,545 --> 00:35:51,898
Must not have meant much if I barely remember.

500
00:35:51,898 --> 00:35:54,588
You said it was life-or-death.
Did you kill him?

501
00:35:54,588 --> 00:35:56,564
Just tell me.

502
00:35:57,470 --> 00:35:59,494
Fine. I killed him.

503
00:35:59,494 --> 00:36:01,259
Brutally.

504
00:36:03,764 --> 00:36:05,021
Wait.

505
00:36:05,021 --> 00:36:06,813
Am I the only one with a past?

506
00:36:06,813 --> 00:36:08,495
I don't have one.

507
00:36:08,495 --> 00:36:11,118
- Really?
- Even if I did, I wouldn't tell you.

508
00:36:11,118 --> 00:36:13,143
It's called respect.

509
00:36:13,143 --> 00:36:16,034
So now I'm the rude one?

510
00:36:16,034 --> 00:36:17,699
You kept asking.

511
00:36:17,699 --> 00:36:20,562
Because you kept spilling.

512
00:36:23,391 --> 00:36:25,735
- But really? No one?
- I said no.

513
00:36:25,735 --> 00:36:28,535
- Was she prettier than me?
- Be careful.

514
00:36:29,747 --> 00:36:31,364
[No Dating on Set]
Morning, sir.

515
00:36:31,364 --> 00:36:33,318
- Hello.
- Hello.

516
00:36:33,977 --> 00:36:35,919
- Hello.
- Hello.

517
00:36:35,919 --> 00:36:38,025
Good morning.

518
00:36:38,025 --> 00:36:39,785
What are you doing?

519
00:36:39,785 --> 00:36:42,349
We've already caught three couples.

520
00:36:42,349 --> 00:36:45,815
They should be working, not dating!

521
00:36:47,502 --> 00:36:49,432
Four couples, actually...

522
00:36:50,502 --> 00:36:54,072
A set with lots of couples has good energy.

523
00:36:54,072 --> 00:36:56,575
Who says that?

524
00:36:56,575 --> 00:36:58,790
It's only good for them.

525
00:36:58,790 --> 00:37:03,693
If you ever catch the staff dating,
report it to us right away.

526
00:37:03,693 --> 00:37:06,006
See you later.

527
00:37:14,700 --> 00:37:17,121
[No Smoking on Set]
[No Dating on Set]

528
00:37:41,502 --> 00:37:43,191
"And then...

529
00:37:43,191 --> 00:37:45,201
I fell in love..."

530
00:38:09,769 --> 00:38:12,223
You're about to drool.

531
00:38:12,911 --> 00:38:15,721
Change the way you look at Nan Young.

532
00:38:15,721 --> 00:38:18,232
No lovesick eyes yet.

533
00:38:18,232 --> 00:38:19,591
What?

534
00:38:19,591 --> 00:38:21,929
I'm not. Yi Jae...

535
00:38:21,929 --> 00:38:22,772
Director Ju.

536
00:38:22,772 --> 00:38:25,460
Drop all the worry, fear, and pain.

537
00:38:25,460 --> 00:38:27,805
You're Moo Gyeom, the carefree young master.

538
00:38:27,805 --> 00:38:29,031
Not an independence fighter.

539
00:38:29,031 --> 00:38:30,493
Got it?

540
00:38:31,890 --> 00:38:34,002
Please keep up the good work.

541
00:38:34,002 --> 00:38:36,077
Thank you.

542
00:38:38,240 --> 00:38:39,551
Moo Gyeom.

543
00:38:39,551 --> 00:38:41,350
Let's talk.

544
00:38:42,929 --> 00:38:45,093
- Hurry.
- Okay.

545
00:38:46,502 --> 00:38:49,086
How are you feeling? You okay?

546
00:38:49,086 --> 00:38:51,189
Of course.

547
00:38:51,189 --> 00:38:52,972
Director Ju.

548
00:38:53,846 --> 00:38:57,623
Even if I went back to where I was,

549
00:38:57,623 --> 00:39:00,293
I'm not the old Oh Ha Na anymore.

550
00:39:00,293 --> 00:39:02,836
I've been reborn.

551
00:39:02,836 --> 00:39:04,188
Life, round two.

552
00:39:04,188 --> 00:39:06,373
Happy birthday.

553
00:39:06,373 --> 00:39:09,343
Even if Nan Young runs out of Wolhajeong,

554
00:39:09,343 --> 00:39:14,126
it means nothing
if Moo Gyeom isn't in that world.

555
00:39:14,126 --> 00:39:18,063
That's why she threw herself in
to save him, right?

556
00:39:18,063 --> 00:39:19,300
Right.

557
00:39:19,300 --> 00:39:23,634
I signed that contract to protect myself.

558
00:39:30,684 --> 00:39:32,477
Come closer.

559
00:39:32,477 --> 00:39:34,556
Who was Yi Jae's ex?

560
00:39:34,556 --> 00:39:37,082
What? Yi Jae's ex?

561
00:39:37,871 --> 00:39:40,091
Keep your voice down.

562
00:39:40,091 --> 00:39:42,174
Which ex, exactly?

563
00:39:42,174 --> 00:39:45,320
- There was more than one?
- Of course.

564
00:39:45,320 --> 00:39:47,760
Just the ones I know...

565
00:39:55,016 --> 00:39:56,591
Enough.

566
00:39:58,791 --> 00:40:02,343
One of them got really famous...

567
00:40:09,348 --> 00:40:10,925
No.

568
00:40:12,027 --> 00:40:13,835
I don't want to know.

569
00:40:14,454 --> 00:40:16,209
What's with him?

570
00:40:35,904 --> 00:40:37,488
That's the look.

571
00:40:37,488 --> 00:40:39,453
Love at first sight.

572
00:40:39,453 --> 00:40:41,356
- Sorry?
- Let's rehearse.

573
00:40:41,356 --> 00:40:43,876
Let's rehearse!

574
00:40:45,967 --> 00:40:47,493
So...

575
00:40:48,406 --> 00:40:49,790
Let's do it.

576
00:40:49,790 --> 00:40:51,393
- Okay.
- Okay.

577
00:40:53,281 --> 00:40:55,221
Ready.

578
00:40:55,221 --> 00:40:56,772
Action!

579
00:40:56,772 --> 00:40:58,581
I don't believe we've met.

580
00:40:58,581 --> 00:41:01,081
I'm Nan Young.

581
00:41:05,428 --> 00:41:07,132
What are you doing?

582
00:41:07,132 --> 00:41:09,395
Grab my wrist.

583
00:41:13,232 --> 00:41:16,027
Too proper. You're not a scholar.

584
00:41:17,805 --> 00:41:19,219
Read it again.

585
00:41:19,219 --> 00:41:21,502
Memorize the action lines too.

586
00:41:22,218 --> 00:41:24,169
Sorry.

587
00:41:24,169 --> 00:41:26,084
I'm sorry.

588
00:41:27,551 --> 00:41:30,097
- Sorry.
- It's okay.

589
00:41:30,097 --> 00:41:32,070
- What do we do?
- Sorry.

590
00:41:32,070 --> 00:41:34,270
Let them work it out.

591
00:41:35,212 --> 00:41:37,424
Let's go again.

592
00:41:37,424 --> 00:41:39,969
Focus a little more, please.

593
00:41:39,969 --> 00:41:41,719
Ready...

594
00:41:41,719 --> 00:41:43,263
Action!

595
00:41:44,651 --> 00:41:47,262
I don't believe we've met.

596
00:41:47,262 --> 00:41:49,815
I'm Nan Young.

597
00:41:57,324 --> 00:42:01,574
Noble young master, you're quite impatient.

598
00:42:01,574 --> 00:42:04,153
Why shouldn't I be?

599
00:42:04,841 --> 00:42:09,127
When your eyes are so full of love for me.

600
00:42:12,350 --> 00:42:14,274
Relax a little.

601
00:42:14,274 --> 00:42:15,570
Cut! Great!

602
00:42:15,570 --> 00:42:17,856
Let's go with that.

603
00:42:39,514 --> 00:42:41,875
<i>The spa date is over.</i>

604
00:42:41,875 --> 00:42:44,733
<i>Of the two people you dated today,</i>

605
00:42:44,733 --> 00:42:48,448
<i>go to the room of the one you like more.</i>

606
00:43:33,051 --> 00:43:34,952
Seo In Uk.

607
00:43:37,078 --> 00:43:39,888
I don't sleep with a guy twice
after a drunken hookup.

608
00:43:39,888 --> 00:43:42,287
Some might call it a stupid rule,

609
00:43:42,287 --> 00:43:46,289
but I've lived by it.

610
00:43:47,451 --> 00:43:49,791
But just now...

611
00:43:49,791 --> 00:43:54,338
we had our second night.

612
00:43:54,338 --> 00:43:56,555
What do you think that means?

613
00:43:56,555 --> 00:43:59,415
That there'll be a third.

614
00:43:59,415 --> 00:44:01,202
Maybe even more.

615
00:44:06,282 --> 00:44:07,913
Okay.

616
00:44:07,913 --> 00:44:10,513
- I'll leave the show.
- No.

617
00:44:10,513 --> 00:44:12,537
Don't.

618
00:44:12,537 --> 00:44:13,570
Sorry?

619
00:44:13,570 --> 00:44:18,155
Our third time will be after this shoot wraps.

620
00:44:18,155 --> 00:44:22,215
So stay the game changer until the end.

621
00:44:24,051 --> 00:44:26,520
The man everyone wants.

622
00:44:28,144 --> 00:44:30,164
What does that even mean?

623
00:44:30,164 --> 00:44:32,140
Five minutes left.

624
00:44:32,786 --> 00:44:35,590
Enjoy your date.

625
00:44:43,497 --> 00:44:46,125
She's so weird.

626
00:44:47,683 --> 00:44:49,103
I love it.

627
00:44:49,783 --> 00:44:52,380
Please wrap everything up within 30 minutes!

628
00:44:52,380 --> 00:44:53,147
- Got it.
- Got it.

629
00:44:53,147 --> 00:44:55,944
The team dinner is optional,
so feel free to join if you'd like.

630
00:44:55,944 --> 00:44:56,955
- Yes.
- Yes.

631
00:44:56,955 --> 00:44:58,999
I shared the location in the group chat.

632
00:44:58,999 --> 00:45:01,726
- Please check it!
- Okay!

633
00:45:04,217 --> 00:45:05,281
Directors!

634
00:45:05,281 --> 00:45:10,867
Geum Seong Moo agreed to make a cameo as Crow!

635
00:45:10,867 --> 00:45:13,047
Isn't that amazing?

636
00:45:15,658 --> 00:45:18,781
What? Geum Seong Moo?

637
00:45:18,781 --> 00:45:21,036
That's great.

638
00:45:21,036 --> 00:45:22,311
Oh, right.

639
00:45:22,311 --> 00:45:23,347
Director Ryu.

640
00:45:23,347 --> 00:45:25,607
What I mentioned earlier...

641
00:45:26,934 --> 00:45:29,254
I don't think this is good news.

642
00:45:32,170 --> 00:45:34,370
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

643
00:45:45,038 --> 00:45:46,568
Is the beer good?

644
00:45:46,568 --> 00:45:49,721
Just have one. You'll be fine.

645
00:45:51,009 --> 00:45:53,595
I'll stick to soda.

646
00:46:04,196 --> 00:46:06,169
- Did you see that?
- What?

647
00:46:16,207 --> 00:46:19,151
So Geum Seong Moo is really doing the cameo?

648
00:46:19,151 --> 00:46:22,319
- Why?
- We did a drama together.

649
00:46:22,319 --> 00:46:25,331
I'm not sure he fits Crow.

650
00:46:25,331 --> 00:46:27,882
Guess you had beef with him too.

651
00:46:27,882 --> 00:46:28,544
What?

652
00:46:28,544 --> 00:46:31,408
I hear you always have issues
with male co-stars.

653
00:46:31,408 --> 00:46:33,706
Getting along with them is part of the job.

654
00:46:33,706 --> 00:46:36,959
Jeez... You sound just like my mom.

655
00:46:39,103 --> 00:46:42,346
If he were easy to get along with, I would've.

656
00:46:42,346 --> 00:46:45,703
What am I, some thug picking fights everywhere?

657
00:46:45,703 --> 00:46:48,527
She gets along with Yu Geon.

658
00:46:49,468 --> 00:46:52,118
You've already had six pieces.

659
00:46:52,832 --> 00:46:54,886
You need to watch yourself during shoots.

660
00:46:54,886 --> 00:46:57,497
You think good genes last forever?

661
00:46:57,497 --> 00:46:59,083
Yes, ma'am.

662
00:46:59,083 --> 00:47:01,669
That damn "ma'am."

663
00:47:01,669 --> 00:47:03,318
You call that getting along?

664
00:47:03,318 --> 00:47:05,263
Seems sweet to her.

665
00:47:06,065 --> 00:47:08,411
Lucky you, Yu Geon.

666
00:47:08,411 --> 00:47:10,746
You love Seong Moo.

667
00:47:15,107 --> 00:47:16,608
You mean the Hong Kong actor, huh?

668
00:47:16,608 --> 00:47:20,439
His Korean name is Geum Seong Moo too...

669
00:47:21,344 --> 00:47:22,475
So what?

670
00:47:22,475 --> 00:47:25,179
I meant the Korean actor, Geum Seong Moo.

671
00:47:25,179 --> 00:47:27,937
- Is that his real name?
- Yeah, it is.

672
00:47:31,025 --> 00:47:32,528
You know him well?

673
00:47:32,528 --> 00:47:36,125
Oh, are you a fan of his too?

674
00:47:36,880 --> 00:47:38,782
That hurts.

675
00:47:38,782 --> 00:47:42,201
"Contract Marriage" aired against his
and got crushed in ratings.

676
00:47:42,201 --> 00:47:44,025
Oh, right.

677
00:47:44,025 --> 00:47:47,005
He's huge right now because of that drama.

678
00:47:47,005 --> 00:47:50,038
Everybody loves him.

679
00:47:50,958 --> 00:47:53,138
Lucky you.

680
00:47:53,138 --> 00:47:54,946
Let's keep work and feelings separate.

681
00:47:54,946 --> 00:47:56,772
You seem the worst at that.

682
00:47:56,772 --> 00:47:59,386
And you're so good at it?

683
00:48:02,109 --> 00:48:05,049
I'm trying, ma'am.

684
00:48:06,903 --> 00:48:09,240
I should go.

685
00:48:11,302 --> 00:48:13,414
Let's go, Chae Yeon.

686
00:48:18,785 --> 00:48:21,071
Why did she even come to dinner?

687
00:48:21,071 --> 00:48:22,823
To pick a fight, apparently.

688
00:48:22,823 --> 00:48:25,773
Moo Gyeom! Have a drink with me.

689
00:48:25,773 --> 00:48:27,941
That's okay, right?

690
00:48:27,941 --> 00:48:30,052
Have a little.

691
00:48:30,052 --> 00:48:31,796
Just a little.

692
00:48:31,796 --> 00:48:34,506
I'll drink a lot.

693
00:48:34,506 --> 00:48:36,442
Cheers!

694
00:48:45,288 --> 00:48:47,592
A little would've been fine...

695
00:48:47,592 --> 00:48:49,592
Another soju, please!

696
00:48:56,765 --> 00:48:59,182
Sim Yu Geon.

697
00:48:59,182 --> 00:49:02,283
Even I'm naturally gifted,
and I still work hard.

698
00:49:03,143 --> 00:49:07,105
You think this dewy glow maintains itself?

699
00:49:28,932 --> 00:49:31,344
He even drank?

700
00:49:38,009 --> 00:49:40,379
- Good night!
- Bye.

701
00:49:43,419 --> 00:49:44,426
<i>Want to take a walk?</i>

702
00:49:44,426 --> 00:49:48,457
Any couple I catch
sneaking out tonight is dead meat.

703
00:49:51,327 --> 00:49:53,351
<i>I'll come to your room later.</i>

704
00:49:53,351 --> 00:49:55,792
A walk is at least innocent.

705
00:49:55,792 --> 00:49:58,808
Patrol the halls.

706
00:49:58,808 --> 00:50:00,416
Exactly.

707
00:50:00,416 --> 00:50:04,427
There's definitely a couple on our floor.

708
00:50:04,427 --> 00:50:06,147
Really?

709
00:50:07,054 --> 00:50:08,864
Sharp.

710
00:50:08,864 --> 00:50:11,424
Ye Seo, you take the lower floors.

711
00:50:11,424 --> 00:50:13,198
I'll take upstairs.

712
00:50:13,198 --> 00:50:15,027
Me?

713
00:50:15,027 --> 00:50:17,090
No, thanks.

714
00:50:17,090 --> 00:50:19,767
I thought you were anti-dating.

715
00:50:19,767 --> 00:50:22,087
I'm against it,

716
00:50:22,087 --> 00:50:25,840
but you can't just tell love to stop.

717
00:50:25,840 --> 00:50:27,931
Right... Leave them.

718
00:50:27,931 --> 00:50:30,524
They'll break up when filming wraps.

719
00:50:30,524 --> 00:50:35,808
Exactly. Then why date at work
if they'll break up anyway?

720
00:50:35,808 --> 00:50:37,988
I won't let anyone off.

721
00:50:38,957 --> 00:50:40,341
- Good night!
- Good night.

722
00:50:40,341 --> 00:50:41,962
- Rest up.
- Yeah.

723
00:50:41,962 --> 00:50:44,621
- Good night.
- Sleep tight.

724
00:50:45,603 --> 00:50:47,696
<i>The doors are closing.</i>

725
00:50:48,410 --> 00:50:49,990
Hey.

726
00:50:50,963 --> 00:50:52,720
He looks wasted.

727
00:50:52,720 --> 00:50:54,667
Shouldn't we walk him to his room?

728
00:50:54,667 --> 00:50:56,451
Is he a kid?

729
00:50:56,451 --> 00:50:58,805
Sim Yu Geon. What floor?

730
00:50:58,805 --> 00:51:01,597
- Sixth.
- Seriously...

731
00:51:01,597 --> 00:51:03,984
- Let's go.
- Hey!

732
00:51:07,983 --> 00:51:09,925
Woo Soo Bin...

733
00:51:09,925 --> 00:51:13,092
You're dead when Seong Moo gets here.

734
00:51:22,829 --> 00:51:25,548
Wait! The keycard!

735
00:51:25,548 --> 00:51:27,336
I have it.

736
00:52:58,074 --> 00:53:00,567
Why won't it open...

737
00:53:01,977 --> 00:53:03,753
Come on.

738
00:53:12,254 --> 00:53:14,154
A ghost?

739
00:53:27,675 --> 00:53:30,495
That's your transit card.

740
00:53:30,495 --> 00:53:32,567
Where's your keycard?

741
00:53:34,759 --> 00:53:36,529
Is this a dream?

742
00:53:36,529 --> 00:53:38,249
Move.

743
00:53:52,111 --> 00:53:53,942
I'm sorry.

744
00:53:56,717 --> 00:53:59,776
There's so much I want to say...

745
00:54:01,892 --> 00:54:04,331
But this is all I can say.

746
00:54:04,331 --> 00:54:06,021
Sorry.

747
00:54:09,747 --> 00:54:12,553
What else do you want to say?

748
00:54:15,235 --> 00:54:17,409
I like you.

749
00:54:21,313 --> 00:54:24,143
Even saying that hurts.

750
00:54:26,201 --> 00:54:28,907
Guess I'm really paying for it.

751
00:54:35,810 --> 00:54:40,564
You won't remember this, will you?

752
00:54:40,564 --> 00:54:44,657
Do you want me to?

753
00:54:47,566 --> 00:54:49,700
Tell me to, and I will.

754
00:54:50,517 --> 00:54:53,190
Tell me not to, and I won't.

755
00:55:01,918 --> 00:55:03,855
I know

756
00:55:04,529 --> 00:55:07,426
there's something between us.

757
00:55:08,204 --> 00:55:10,930
So keep liking me.

758
00:55:11,830 --> 00:55:13,851
And pay for it.

759
00:55:32,652 --> 00:55:37,032
I'll remember.

760
00:55:42,444 --> 00:55:43,641
Stop!

761
00:55:43,641 --> 00:55:45,084
Hey!

762
00:55:51,241 --> 00:55:53,728
Cut! Hold on.

763
00:55:55,597 --> 00:55:56,975
Sir.

764
00:55:56,975 --> 00:56:01,084
Could we go handheld up to this alley?

765
00:56:01,084 --> 00:56:03,545
You're kidding, right?

766
00:56:03,545 --> 00:56:06,078
You want me running with the camera?

767
00:56:06,078 --> 00:56:08,637
No. The blocking's too tight.

768
00:56:08,637 --> 00:56:10,514
The crew will keep getting in frame.

769
00:56:10,514 --> 00:56:14,714
I want the audience
to feel chased with Moo Gyeom.

770
00:56:14,714 --> 00:56:20,421
The tension has to peak
for Crow's rescue to land.

771
00:56:20,421 --> 00:56:22,051
Let's try it once in rehearsal.

772
00:56:22,051 --> 00:56:25,439
If it doesn't work, I'll drop it.

773
00:56:28,105 --> 00:56:29,682
Fine.

774
00:56:29,682 --> 00:56:31,362
Thank you.

775
00:56:32,022 --> 00:56:33,658
Let's go handheld.

776
00:56:33,658 --> 00:56:36,638
Producer Nam! Where are you now?

777
00:56:36,638 --> 00:56:38,962
The actor is here...

778
00:56:45,849 --> 00:56:47,366
Yi Jae!

779
00:56:48,282 --> 00:56:50,749
Oh my gosh. You okay?

780
00:56:50,749 --> 00:56:52,903
Who did this?

781
00:57:07,446 --> 00:57:09,268
That was dangerous.

782
00:57:14,536 --> 00:57:15,946
Director Ju.

783
00:57:15,946 --> 00:57:17,773
Seong Moo?

784
00:58:06,526 --> 00:58:08,496
<i>How did you feel hearing about me?</i>

785
00:58:08,496 --> 00:58:10,094
<i>That's enough.</i>

786
00:58:10,094 --> 00:58:12,533
<i>You know what she and I are.</i>

787
00:58:12,533 --> 00:58:15,456
<i>That you were her first love?</i>

788
00:58:15,456 --> 00:58:16,600
<i>I love you.</i>

789
00:58:16,600 --> 00:58:18,213
<i>You don't remember that day?</i>

790
00:58:18,213 --> 00:58:19,366
<i>Stop drinking.</i>

791
00:58:19,366 --> 00:58:21,603
<i>I want to see what you'll do if I get drunk.</i>

792
00:58:21,603 --> 00:58:23,360
<i>It's just us here.</i>

793
00:58:23,360 --> 00:58:24,610
<i>So be honest.</i>

794
00:58:24,610 --> 00:58:26,211
<i>Remember this place?</i>

795
00:58:26,211 --> 00:58:30,030
<i>I liked you ten years ago, and I still do.</i>

796
00:58:30,030 --> 00:58:33,058
<i>You're still hung up on your first love?</i>

